{
  "schema": 1,
  "description": "The repository settings standard, keyed by repository kind, applied and checked by tools/repo_settings.py. The repositories block lists each repository with the values its description, homepage and topics are built from; an overrides block there replaces individual settings of its kind. ruleset protects the default branch; mergeRuleset is the second ruleset of a repository that gives contributors write access: one update rule, bypassed by the Repository admin role (actor_id 5) on pull requests only, so nobody pushes to main and only the owner merges. environments names each deployment environment with the branches its deployment branch policy allows (null: every branch) and the secrets it holds; the publishing key lives in `publish`, allowed to main only, never as a repository secret.",
  "kinds": {
    "source": {
